   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Stunned by Dmitry Nagiyev's announcement, Chef Viktor asks how Kristina can run the restaurant. Nagiyev praises her management studies and reminds everyone that she worked at Claude Monet for a whole year. Let's listen to their exchange in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "В смысле?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Ну, в прямом смысле.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Она умная и красивая.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Но это ведь сложная работа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Она изучала управление ресторанами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "А потом она здесь работала.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Она работала в нашем ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Да, она работала здесь целый год.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Да, я хорошо помню это время.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "В общем, прошу любить и жаловать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вот ваше новое начальство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Добро пожаловать, Кристина Семёновна.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's walk through this exchange line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "В смысле?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do you mean?' Chef Viktor can hardly believe what he just heard.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Ну, в прямом смысле.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, in the literal sense.' Here, Nagiyev confirms he is completely serious.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Она умная и красивая.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She is smart and beautiful.' He begins listing his wife's qualifications.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Но это ведь сложная работа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But this is difficult work.' Viktor points out how demanding the restaurant business is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Она изучала управление ресторанами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She studied restaurant management.' Here, Nagiyev notes that Kristina studied hospitality management.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "А потом она здесь работала.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And then she worked here.' He reminds the team of her past experience at Claude Monet.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Она работала в нашем ресторане?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did she work in our restaurant?' Rising intonation turns the statement into a surprised question.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "Да, она работала здесь целый год.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, she worked here for a whole year.' Here, Nagiyev emphasizes that she spent a full year working there.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Да, я хорошо помню это время.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I remember that time well.' Viktor recalls the days before Kristina married the owner.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ilya",
   "t": "В общем, прошу любить и жаловать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'In short, please welcome and respect her.' This classic Russian idiom means 'please give her a warm welcome'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вот ваше новое начальство.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here is your new boss.' Here, Nagiyev officially hands authority over to Kristina.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Добро пожаловать, Кристина Семёновна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
